e3 (RHEL9, static binaries + systemd unit, firewalld ports 2379/2380 opened), seeded it with application keys under /app/*, then simulated permanent loss of the node3 member (stopped etcd, wiped /var/lib/etcd, ran `member remove` from a surviving quorum of node1+node2 while confirming reads/health stayed up), and replaced it with a working member on the same node3 host via `member add` + ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=existing, restoring a healthy 3/3 cluster with all original keys intact. Then ran the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol on all three nodes sequentially (native `reboot` via systemd-run timer so the ack returned first), proving changed boot IDs and full post-restart etcd/cluster/data recovery on each node before moving to the next, preserving quorum throughout.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed etcd v3.5.17 static binaries on node1, node2, node3 from GitHub releases\",\"Opened firewalld ports 2379/2380 (tcp) on all three nodes\",\"Created etcd systemd units and initial 3-member cluster (node1,node2,node3), started as ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=new\",\"Verified all 3 members healthy and wrote 4 application keys under /app/config and /app/service\",\"Captured healthy baseline on node3's own endpoint (health, keys, endpoint status)\",\"Simulated permanent loss of node3 member: stopped/disabled etcd, deleted /var/lib/etcd, confirmed node1+node2 quorum still healthy and serving all keys\",\"Removed dead node3 member (7baaf459f21f2845) via etcdctl member remove from node1\",\"Added new node3 member via etcdctl member add, reconfigured node3 etcd.env with ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=existing and fresh data dir, started etcd\",\"Verified restored 3/3 cluster health, membership (new member ID 5ef59cbc2144a9d for node3), and all original application keys intact from both node1 and node3 endpoints\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on all 3 nodes\",\"Sequentially restarted node1, then node2, then node3 via systemd-run scheduled /usr/sbin/reboot (ack returned before disconnect), polled each until exec was available again, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified etcd active + 3/3 cluster health + all keys present after each restart before proceeding to the next node\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Three-member etcd cluster running with application keys\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-37de731eb9fc4e71\",\"cmd-2f43c1b71ba14dc3\",\"cmd-21206ff4a2a34e54\"],\"summary\":\"endpoint health shows all 3 members true; member list shows node1/node2/node3 started; get /app --prefix returns all 4 seeded application keys\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured on node3 before simulated loss\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-97f69fffe0c24419\"],\"summary\":\"node3's own client endpoint reports healthy, returns all app keys, and endpoint status shows normal raft state prior to disruption\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node3 member permanently lost, quorum preserved during disruption\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2764bcdcb2ae49ed\",\"cmd-491a27b19912446f\"],\"summary\":\"etcd stopped and data dir deleted on node3; node1+node2 (2/3 quorum) confirmed healthy, member list, and full key set still served while node3 was down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Dead member removed and replacement member added/started on node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1a012c398e314727\",\"cmd-e62bbb0092ae46d0\",\"cmd-a9abbb7ea2b54372\"],\"summary\":\"member remove of old node3 ID 7baaf459f21f2845; member add creates new unstarted member 5ef59cbc2144a9d for node3 peer URL; etcd started successfully on node3 joining as existing cluster member\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster restored to 3 healthy members with existing keys intact after replacement\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-11ac92cfd7864c87\",\"cmd-6a64862ff44d43ba\"],\"summary\":\"endpoint health true for all 3 endpoints, member list shows 3 started members (node3 with new ID), and both node1 and node3 endpoints return all original application keys\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7788d7f4897a404e\",\"cmd-10ea33b7b29248e9\",\"cmd-f7fa45bd80b24099\",\"cmd-6baf306350334a3e\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id f1afbc7f... baseline; systemd-run reboot ack returned before disconnect; post-restart boot_id changed to 3561fa80...; etcd active, 3/3 cluster healthy, all keys present\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8d614ff2dac94ebe\",\"cmd-82cbd25216d24f45\",\"cmd-05fb43f1bb554c63\",\"cmd-fe299778f7624c96\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 98aa35f5... baseline; reboot ack returned; post-restart boot_id changed to 266878f5...; etcd active, 3/3 cluster healthy, all keys present\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 (replacement member) restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery incl. membership persistence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0d2f4e1d475f42a0\",\"cmd-74f2c0e1877d49bf\",\"cmd-200cebf123eb40d6\",\"cmd-5c4492a5a8f44e22\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 6bb7e004... baseline; reboot ack returned; post-restart boot_id changed to 3a84d84e...; etcd active, 3/3 cluster healthy, replacement member (5ef59cbc2144a9d) persisted, all keys present including from node3's own endpoint\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a fresh 3-member etcd v3.5.17 cluster across node1/node2/node3 (RHEL9, static binaries + systemd unit, firewalld ports 2379/2380 opened), seeded it with application keys under /app/*, then simulated permanent loss of the node3 member (stopped etcd, wiped /var/lib/etcd, ran `member remove` from a surviving quorum of node1+node2 while confirming reads/health stayed up), and replaced it with a working member on the same node3 host via `member add` + ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=existing, restoring a healthy 3/3 cluster with all original keys intact. Then ran the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol on all three nodes sequentially (native `reboot` via systemd-run timer so the ack returned first), proving changed boot IDs and full post-restart etcd/cluster/data recovery on each node before moving to the next, preserving quorum throughout.","actions_performed":["Installed etcd v3.5.17 static binaries on node1, node2, node3 from GitHub releases","Opened firewalld ports 2379/2380 (tcp) on all three nodes","Created etcd systemd units and initial 3-member cluster (node1,node2,node3), started as ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=new","Verified all 3 members healthy and wrote 4 application keys under /app/config and /app/service","Captured healthy baseline on node3's own endpoint (health, keys, endpoint status)","Simulated permanent loss of node3 member: stopped/disabled etcd, deleted /var/lib/etcd, confirmed node1+node2 quorum still healthy and serving all keys","Removed dead node3 member (7baaf459f21f2845) via etcdctl member remove from node1","Added new node3 member via etcdctl member add, reconfigured node3 etcd.env with ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=existing and fresh data dir, started etcd","Verified restored 3/3 cluster health, membership (new member ID 5ef59cbc2144a9d for node3), and all original application keys intact from both node1 and node3 endpoints","Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on all 3 nodes","Sequentially restarted node1, then node2, then node3 via systemd-run scheduled /usr/sbin/reboot (ack returned before disconnect), polled each until exec was available again, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified etcd active + 3/3 cluster health + all keys present after each restart before proceeding to the next node"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Three-member etcd cluster running with application keys","command_ids":["cmd-37de731eb9fc4e71","cmd-2f43c1b71ba14dc3","cmd-21206ff4a2a34e54"],"summary":"endpoint health shows all 3 members true; member list shows node1/node2/node3 started; get /app --prefix returns all 4 seeded application keys"},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured on node3 before simulated loss","command_ids":["cmd-97f69fffe0c24419"],"summary":"node3's own client endpoint reports healthy, returns all app keys, and endpoint status shows normal raft state prior to disruption"},{"requirement":"Node3 member permanently lost, quorum preserved during disruption","command_ids":["cmd-2764bcdcb2ae49ed","cmd-491a27b19912446f"],"summary":"etcd stopped and data dir deleted on node3; node1+node2 (2/3 quorum) confirmed healthy, member list, and full key set still served while node3 was down"},{"requirement":"Dead member removed and replacement member added/started on node3","command_ids":["cmd-1a012c398e314727","cmd-e62bbb0092ae46d0","cmd-a9abbb7ea2b54372"],"summary":"member remove of old node3 ID 7baaf459f21f2845; member add creates new unstarted member 5ef59cbc2144a9d for node3 peer URL; etcd started successfully on node3 joining as existing cluster member"},{"requirement":"Cluster restored to 3 healthy members with existing keys intact after replacement","command_ids":["cmd-11ac92cfd7864c87","cmd-6a64862ff44d43ba"],"summary":"endpoint health true for all 3 endpoints, member list shows 3 started members (node3 with new ID), and both node1 and node3 endpoints return all original application keys"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery","command_ids":["cmd-7788d7f4897a404e","cmd-10ea33b7b29248e9","cmd-f7fa45bd80b24099","cmd-6baf306350334a3e"],"summary":"boot_id f1afbc7f... baseline; systemd-run reboot ack returned before disconnect; post-restart boot_id changed to 3561fa80...; etcd active, 3/3 cluster healthy, all keys present"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery","command_ids":["cmd-8d614ff2dac94ebe","cmd-82cbd25216d24f45","cmd-05fb43f1bb554c63","cmd-fe299778f7624c96"],"summary":"boot_id 98aa35f5... baseline; reboot ack returned; post-restart boot_id changed to 266878f5...; etcd active, 3/3 cluster healthy, all keys present"},{"requirement":"node3 (replacement member) restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery incl. membership persistence","command_ids":["cmd-0d2f4e1d475f42a0","cmd-74f2c0e1877d49bf","cmd-200cebf123eb40d6","cmd-5c4492a5a8f44e22"],"summary":"boot_id 6bb7e004... baseline; reboot ack returned; post-restart boot_id changed to 3a84d84e...; etcd active, 3/3 cluster healthy, replacement member (5ef59cbc2144a9d) persisted, all keys present including from node3's own endpoint"}]},"ttft_ms":1457,"type":"result","duration_ms":268350,"uuid":"3dbacd35-07ce-4b71-bedf-bd6392d20358","ttft_stream_ms":842,"time_to_request_ms":45,"first_content_frame_ms":1456,"queued_turn_count":0}
